lowing workaround\n        ...\n```\n\nIt might reference `self._downloader.params.get('prefer_free_formats')`. Let me check with get_info.\n\nAlso `url_result` - returns a dict with `_type: 'url'`, `url`, `ie_key`. It may call `self._downloader`? Let me check:\n\n```python\ndef url_result(self, url, ie=None, video_id=None, video_title=None):\n    \"\"\"Returns a url that points to a page that should be processed\"\"\"\n    # TODO: PEP 8 (two blank lines)\n    if video_id is None:\n        video_id = self._generic_id(url)\n    if video_title is not None:\n        video_id = '%s %s' % (video_id, video_title)\n    entry = {\n        '_type': 'url',\n        'url': url,\n        'id': video_id,\n    }\n    if ie is not None:\n        entry['ie_key'] = ie\n    return entry\n```\n\nThat's fine, no downloader needed.\n\n`_match_id` uses `self._match_valid_url(url)` which uses `_VALID_URL`. Fine.\n\nLet me check `_sort_formats` in youtube_dl. I'll use get_info.\n\nAlso, `_download_webpage` signature: `def _download_webpage(self, url_or_request, video_id, note=None, errnote=None, fatal=True, tries=1, timeout=5.0, data=None, headers={}, query={}, expected_status=None)`. We'll monkeypatch it.\n\nLet me now design the tests.\n\nTest A: youtube branch (options path)\n- page HTML contains `var options = {...};` where the JSON (after js_to_json) parses to a dict with 'video': {'youtube': 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xxx'}, 'title': 'Test Title', 'poster': 'https://example.com/poster.jpg'.\n- Note: `js_to_json` converts single-quoted keys to double quotes etc. Actually `options_str` is like `{'video': {'youtube': '...'}, 'title': '...', 'poster': '...'}`. `js_to_json` converts it to valid JSON. Then `_parse_json` parses it.\n- Assert result == {'_type': 'url', 'url': 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xxx', 'id': ..., 'ie_key': 'Youtube'}\n\nWait, `url_result` with video_id=None calls `self._generic_id(url)`. Let me check `_generic_id`:\n\n```python\n@staticmethod\ndef _generic_