lt=None` path). To cover it, I could have a fallback page WITHOUT a poster key. Let me add that as a variation \u2014 maybe in the m3u8/f4m test, omit poster? But then I don't test the poster regex match in fallback... Hmm, I have two fallback-ish scenarios I could do:\n\nTest 3: fallback with m3u8 + f4m, WITH poster \u2192 covers lines 55-60 fully (poster regex matches).\nTest 4 (optional): fallback without poster \u2192 covers the `default=None` branch of line 59-60.\n\nHmm, the `default=None` is inside `_html_search_regex` \u2014 the branch is in common.py, not in udn.py. Coverage of udn.py lines 59-60 is achieved either way (the line executes). The \"branch\" within line 60 (default used or not) is in common.py. The task says \"execute all missing lines and branches\" \u2014 branches of udn.py. Line 60 executes in both cases. I think one fallback test with poster present is enough, but adding a no-poster variant is cheap and tests `thumbnail: None`. Maybe I'll fold it in: actually, let me keep tests focused. I'll do:\n\n1. test_youtube_result (options path, youtube branch, early return)\n2. test_options_path_with_mp4_formats (options path, mp4 branch with regex match + no match + empty url skip)\n3. test_fallback_path_with_m3u8_and_f4m (fallback path, m3u8 branch, f4m branch)\n\nThat covers:\n- 42, 44, 46-49: all tests\n- 50-53 (if options): tests 1, 2\n- 55-60 (else): test 3\n- 62-63 (youtube): test 1\n- 65-66 (loop): tests 2, 3\n- 67-68 (continue): test 2\n- 70-72: tests 2, 3\n- 75-77 (m3u8): test 3\n- 78-80 (f4m): test 3\n- 82-87 (else): test 2\n- 88-91 (mobj): test 2 (1080p format)\n- 93 (append): tests 2, 3\n- 95 (sort): tests 2, 3\n- 97-101 (return): tests 2, 3\n\nAll lines 42-101 covered. \n\nNow, one thing to double check in test 3: the m3u8 URL 'https://cdn.example.com/master.m3u8' \u2014 `determine_ext` \u2192 'm3u8'. Good. f4m: 'https://cdn.example.com/manifest.f4m' \u2192 'f4m'. Good.\n\nBut wait \u2014 in test 3, the loop order: video_urls = {'hls': '/api/hls', 'hds': '/api/hds'} \u2014 from JSON parse, order preserved: hls first, hds second. calls: [PAGE_URL, api/hls, api/hds]. Good.\n\nNow, the mocked `_extract_m3u8_formats` returns a list with one format dict. `_sort_formats` will process it: `f.get('ext')` = 'mp4' (fine), protocol = 'm3u8' (provided). Key: preference 0, vcodec=='none' \u2192 False, height is None \u2192 False, height 720, tbr is None \u2192 False, tbr 2000, acodec=='none' \u2192 False, abr is None \u2192 True, abr None, ext in ('f4f','f4m') \u2192 False, filesize is None \u2192 True, filesize None. OK, comparable.\n\nFor hds format: height 360, tbr 500, protocol 'f4m', ext 'flv'. Key: (0, False, False, 360, False, 500, False, True, None, False, True, None).\n\nCompare hds vs hls: (0, False, False, 360, ...) vs (0, False, False, 720, ...) \u2192 hds < hls. Sorted: [hds-360, hls-720]. So the f4m format first, m3u8 last. If I assert order, formats[0]['format_id'] == 'hds-360' and formats[1]['format_id'] == 'hls-720'. But this depends on `_sort_formats` implementation. Let me verify via get_info first.\n\nHmm, also \u2014 wait, there's a potential issue with `_sort_formats` and the `preference` key: `f.get('preference')` \u2014 if None \u2192 0. Fine.\n\nAnother potential issue: in older youtube-dl versions, `_sort_formats` might be:\n\n```python\ndef _sort_formats(self, formats, field_preference=None):\n    if not formats:\n        raise ExtractorError('No video formats found!')\n    ...\n    formats.sort(key=...)\n```\n\nwith `self._downloader.params.get('prefer_free_formats')` inside. Either way, fake downloader with params dict handles it.\n\nHmm, but what if `_sort_formats` in this version doesn't touch `self._downloader` at all? Then FakeDownloader is harmless. Either way, providing a fake downloader with `params={}` is safe. But careful: if `_sort_formats` calls `self._downloader.params.get(...)` and my FakeDownloader has params={}, `.get('prefer_free_formats')` \u2192 None \u2192 falsy \u2192 else branch. Good.\n\nNow \u2014 `InfoExtractor.__init__` \u2014 let me check whether it accepts downloader positionally. `def __init__(self, downloader=None)`. `UDNEmbedIE(FakeDownloader())` \u2192 fine. Or I can do `ie = UDNEmbedIE(); ie._downloader = FakeDownloader()`. Hmm, but if __init__ sets other attrs, fine.\n\nWait, actually there might be an issue: in some versions, `InfoExtractor.__init__` is:\n\n```python\ndef __init__(self, downloader=None):\n    self._ready = False\n    self._downloader = downloader\n    self._x_forwarded_for_ip = None\n```\n\nHmm, `self._x_forwarded_for_ip` \u2014 hmm, that might be in newer versions. Whatever, get_info will tell me.\n\nLet me now also think about `url_result` \u2014 it might call `self._downloader`? I don't think so. It builds a dict. But `_generic_id` \u2014 let me check.\n\nOK, let me make the get_info calls now. I'll batch them all in one block:\n\n- UDNEmbedIE._VALID_URL\n- InfoExtractor.__init__\n- InfoExtractor._match_id\n- InfoExtractor._download_webpage\n- InfoExtractor._html_search_regex\n- InfoExtractor._parse_json\n- InfoExtractor.url_result\n- InfoExtractor._generic_id\n- InfoExtractor._extract_m3u8_formats\n- InfoExtractor._extract_f4m_formats\n- InfoExtractor._sort_formats\n- InfoExtractor.report_warning\n- InfoExtractor.to_screen\n- js_to_json\n- determine_ext\n\nThat's 15 calls. Maybe that's too many; let me prioritize: _sort_formats (critical), __init__ (critical), url_result/_generic_id (for assertions), _VALID_URL (for URL), js_to_json (for page construction), _parse_json (fatal=False behavior), report_warning/to_screen (for fake downloader), _extract_m3u8_formats/_extract_f4m_formats (signatures for mocks), _match_id, _download_webpage, _html_search_regex, determine_ext.\n\nI'll do them all in one batch \u2014 the instructions say to batch independent calls.\n\nThen write the final test.\n\nLet me pre-draft the final test file:\n\n```python\nimport pytest\n\nfrom youtube_dl.extractor.udn import UDNEmbedIE\n\nPAGE_URL = 'https://video.udn.com/embed/news/300040'\nVIDEO_ID = '300040'\n\n\nclass FakeDownloader(object):\n    \"\"\"Minimal stand-in for YoutubeDL: only what InfoExtractor touches.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.params = {}\n        self.messages = []\n\n    def to_screen(self, msg):\n        self.messages.append(msg)\n\n    def report_warning(self, msg):\n        self.messages.append(msg)\n\n\ndef _install_download_stub(monkeypatch, ie, responses):\n    \"\"\"Replace _download_webpage with a lookup table; returns recorded URLs.\"\"\"\n    requested = []\n\n    def fake_download_webpage(url_or_request, video_id, *args, **kwargs):\n        url = str(url_or_request)\n        requested.append(url)\n        if url not in responses:\n            raise AssertionError('Unexpected _download_webpage call for %r' % url)\n        return responses[url]\n\n    monkeypatch.setattr(ie, '_download_webpage', fake_download_webpage)\n    return requested\n\n\ndef _make_ie(monkeypatch, responses):\n    ie = UDNEmbedIE(FakeDownloader())\n    requested = _install_download_stub(monkeypatch, ie, responses)\n    return ie, requested\n\n\ndef test_youtube_link_short_circuits_format_extraction(monkeypatch):\n    page = (\n        '<html><body><script>'\n        \"var options = {'video': {'youtube': 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BaW_jenozKc'},\"\n        \" 'title': 'YT Title', 'poster': 'https://example.com/poster.jpg'};\"\n        '</script></body></html>'\n    )\n    ie, requested = _make_ie(monkeypatch, {PAGE_URL: page})\n\n    result = ie._real_extract(PAGE_URL)\n\n    assert result['_type'] == 'url'\n    assert result['url'] == 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BaW_jenozKc'\n    assert result['ie_key'] == 'Youtube'\n    # Only the embed page itself was fetched; no per-format requests.\n    assert requested == [PAGE_URL]\n\n\ndef test_options_dict_builds_http_formats(monkeypatch):\n    page = (\n        '<html><body><script>'\n        \"var options = {'video': {'mp4_1080': '/api/1080', 'mp4_broken': '', 'mp4_other': '/api/other'},\"\n        \" 'title': 'Test Title', 'poster': 'https://example.com/poster.jpg'};\"\n        '</script></body></html>'\n    )\n    responses = {\n        PAGE_URL: page,\n        'https://video.udn.com/api/1080': 'https://cdn.example.com/video_1080p_4000.mp4',\n        'https://video.udn.com/api/other': 'https://cdn.example.com/video.mp4',\n    }\n    ie, requested = _make_ie(monkeypatch, responses)\n\n    result = ie._real_extract(PAGE_URL)\n\n    assert result['id'] == VIDEO_ID\n    assert result['title'] == 'Test Title'\n    assert result['thumbnail'] == 'https://example.com/poster.jpg'\n\n    formats = result['formats']\n    assert len(formats) == 2  # the entry whose URL is '' must be skipped\n    by_id = {fmt['format_id']: fmt for fmt in formats}\n    assert set(by_id) == {'http-mp4_1080', 'http-mp4_other'}\n\n    high = by_id['http-mp4_1080']\n    assert high['url'] == 'https://cdn.example.com/video_1080p_4000.mp4'\n    assert high['height'] == 1080\n    assert high['tbr'] == 4000\n\n    plain = by_id['http-mp4_other']\n    assert plain['url'] == 'https://cdn.example.com/video.mp4'\n    assert 'height' not in plain\n    assert 'tbr' not in plain\n\n    # _sort_formats puts the highest quality last\n    assert formats[-1]['format_id'] == 'http-mp4_1080'\n\n    assert requested[0] == PAGE_URL\n    assert set(requested[1:]) == {\n        'https://video.udn.com/api/1080',\n        'https://video.udn.com/api/other',\n    }\n    assert len(requested) == 3\n\n\ndef test_unparseable_options_falls_back_to_regexes(monkeypatch):\n    page = (\n        '<html><body><script>'\n        'var options = {'\n        '\"video\": {\"hls\": \"/api/hls\", \"hds\": \"/api/hds\"}, '\n        \"title: 'Fallback Title', \"\n        \"poster: 'https://example.com/fallback.jpg', \"\n        'autoplay: yes'\n        '};'\n        '</script></body></html>'\n    )\n    responses = {\n        PAGE_URL: page,\n        'https://video.udn.com/api/hls': 'https://cdn.example.com/master.m3u8',\n        'https://video.udn.com/api/hds': 'https://cdn.example.com/manifest.f4m',\n    }\n    ie, requested = _make_ie(monkeypatch, responses)\n\n    m3u8_calls = []\n\n    def fake_m3u8(video_url, video_id, *args, **kwargs):\n        m3u8_calls.append((video_url, video_id, kwargs))\n        return [{\n            'format_id': 'hls-720',\n            'url': 'https://cdn.example.com/hls-720.mp4',\n            'ext': 'mp4',\n            'height': 720,\n            'tbr': 2000,\n            'protocol': 'm3u8',\n        }]\n\n    f4m_calls = []\n\n    def fake_f4m(video_url, video_id, *args, **kwargs):\n        f4m_calls.append((video_url, video_id, kwargs))\n        return [{\n            'format_id': 'hds-360',\n            'url': 'https://cdn.example.com/hds-360.flv',\n            'ext': 'flv',\n            'height': 360,\n            'tbr': 500,\n            'protocol': 'f4m',\n        }]\n\n    monkeypatch.setattr(ie, '_extract_m3u8_formats', fake_m3u8)\n    monkeypatch.setattr(ie, '_extract_f4m_formats', fake_f4m)\n\n    result = ie._real_extract(PAGE_URL)\n\n    assert result['id'] == VIDEO_ID\n    assert result['title'] == 'Fallback Title'\n    assert result['thumbnail'] == 'https://example.com/fallback.jpg'\n\n    formats = result['formats']\n    assert {fmt['format_id'] for fmt in formats} == {'hls-720', 'hds-360'}\n    assert formats[-1]['format_id'] == 'hls-720'  # sorted best-last\n\n    assert m3u8_calls == [(\n        'https://cdn.example.com/master.m3u8',\n        VIDEO_ID,\n        {'ext': 'mp4', 'm3u8_id': 'hls'},\n    )]\n    assert f4m_calls == [(\n        'https://cdn.example.com/manifest.f4m',\n        VIDEO_ID,\n        {'f4m_id': 'hds'},\n    )]\n\n    assert requested[0] == PAGE_URL\n    assert set(requested[1:]) == {\n        'https://video.udn.com/api/hls',\n        'https://video.udn.com/api/hds',\n    }\n```\n\nWait, in test 3, the kwargs for `_extract_m3u8_f