` \u2192 similar \u2713. options truthy \u2192 youtube branch \u2713.\n\nNow the FALLBACK test options string:\n\n`{\"video\": {\"hls\": \"/api/hls\", \"hds\": \"/api/hds\"}, title: 'Fallback Title', poster: 'https://example.com/fallback.jpg', volume: 2+2}`\n\njs_to_json trace:\n- `\"video\"` \u2014 double-quote alt \u2713 \u2192 fix_kv: v[0]=='\"' \u2192 inner sub on v[1:-1]=`video` \u2014 no escapes/quotes \u2192 `'\"video\"'` \u2713 unchanged.\n- `{\"hls\": \"/api/hls\", \"hds\": \"/api/hds\"}` \u2014 strings unchanged \u2713.\n- `title` \u2014 identifier alt: starts `t` \u2208 [a-df-zA-DF-Z_] \u2713, `[.a-zA-Z_0-9]*` matches `itle` \u2192 v=`title`. fix_kv: not true/false/null; v[0] not quote; INTEGER_TABLE: `(?s)^(0[xX][0-9a-fA-F]+){skip}:?$` \u2014 no; octal \u2014 no \u2192 return `'\"title\"'` \u2713.\n- `'Fallback Title'` \u2192 `\"Fallback Title\"` \u2713\n- `poster` \u2192 `\"poster\"` \u2713\n- `'https://example.com/fallback.jpg'` \u2192 `\"https://example.com/fallback.jpg\"` \u2713\n- `volume` \u2192 `\"volume\"` \u2713\n- `2+2` \u2014 at `2`: alts \u2014 number alts need `0`-prefix or `(?={skip}:)` lookahead; identifier needs letter start; \u2192 no match \u2192 `2+2` untouched \u2713.\n\nResult: `{\"video\": {\"hls\": \"/api/hls\", \"hds\": \"/api/hds\"}, \"title\": \"Fallback Title\", \"poster\": \"https://example.com/fallback.jpg\", \"volume\": 2+2}` \u2192 json.loads FAILS at `2+2` \u2713 \u2192 report_warning \u2192 None \u2192 `or {}` \u2192 else branch \u2713.\n\nThen:\n- video regex on trans_options_str: `\"video\"\\s*:\\s*({.+?})\\s*,` \u2014 trans = `{\"video\": {\"hls\": \"/api/hls\", \"hds\": \"/api/hds\"}, \"title\": ...}`. Match: `\"video\"` then `:` then `({\"hls\": \"/api/hls\", \"hds\": \"/api/hds\"})` then `,` \u2713. group(1) parses \u2713 \u2192 {'hls': '/api/hls', 'hds': '/api/hds'}.\n- title regex on OPTIONS_STR (original): `title\\s*:\\s*'(.+?)'\\s*,` \u2014 original has `title: 'Fallback Title',` \u2713 \u2192 'Fallback Title'.\n- poster regex: `poster\\s*:\\s*'(.+?)'\\s*,` \u2014 `poster: 'https://example.com/fallback.jpg',` \u2713 \u2192 URL.\n\n\u2713 All good. Note: `_html_search_regex` for video urls operates on trans_options_str \u2014 the regex needs `\"video\"` DOUBLE-quoted in trans \u2014 \u2713 since js_to_json quoted... wait, `\"video\"` was ALREADY double-quoted in my options_str. Even better \u2014 no reliance on key-quoting for the video dict. But title/poster keys DID rely on js_to_json quoting? No \u2014 the title/poster regexes run on options_str (ORIGINAL), where they're unquoted `title:` \u2014 the regex `title\\s*:\\s*'` doesn't care about quotes on the key \u2713. And the video regex runs on trans_options_str where `\"video\"` is double-quoted (originally so) \u2713. Robust.\n\nHmm \u2014 one more check on the video regex against trans_options_str: `({.+?})\\s*,` \u2014 non-greedy `.+?` with `(?sx)` flags? `_html_search_regex` compiles with flags=0 (unless passed). `.` won't match `\\n` \u2014 my page is single-line inside the script \u2713. But wait \u2014 the FULL page HTML: `<html><script>var options = {...};</script></html>` \u2014 the regex `\"video\"\\s*:\\s*({.+?})\\s*,` is applied to trans_options_str (just the options substring), not the whole page \u2713.\n\nAnd the options regex `var\\s+options\\s*=\\s*([^;]+);` applied to the PAGE \u2014 `[^;]+` \u2014 my options contain no `;` \u2713. But CAREFUL: `</script></html>` after the `;` \u2014 irrelevant, match ends at first `;` \u2713.\n\nNow \u2014 `_search_regex`/`_html_search_regex` \u2014 need to confirm no downloader dependency on SUCCESS path. Classic impl returns group. I'll verify with get_info to be safe.\n\nNow the remaining verification batch:\n- `UDNEmbedIE._PROTOCOL_RELATIVE_VALID_URL`\n- `InfoExtractor._match_id`\n- `InfoExtractor.set_downloader`\n- `determine_protocol`\n- `InfoExtractor._html_search_regex`\n\nLet me also grab `InfoExtractor._download_webpage` just to be 100% sure about arg names (not needed really). Skip.\n\nAlso `UDNEmbedIE.IE_NAME` \u2014 used in report_warning string formatting \u2014 any string works. Skip.\n\nNow about `_sort_formats` and my formats in test 2 \u2014 I do NOT set 'protocol', so `determine_protocol(f)` runs. Check it handles 'https://...' URLs purely. Classic:\n\n```python\ndef determine_protocol(f):\n    protocol = f.get('protocol')\n    if not protocol:\n        url = f['url']\n        if url.startswith('rtmp'):\n            protocol = 'rtmp'\n            ...\n        else:\n            protocol = compat_urllib_parse_urlparse(url).scheme\n            if not protocol:\n                protocol = 'https' if ... \n    return protocol\n```\n\nPure \u2713. But verify anyway.\n\nOne more consideration for test 2's `_sort_formats` key computation \u2014 `f.get('ext')`: the workaround `if not f.get('ext') and 'url' in f: f['ext'] = determine_ext(f['url'])` \u2014 our formats lack 'ext' \u2192 set from URL: 'video_1080p_4000.mp4' \u2192 'mp4' \u2713; 'video.mp4' \u2192 'mp4' \u2713. Then `preference`: ext 'mp4' not in ['f4f','f4m'] \u2192 0. protocol \u2192 'https' \u2192 proto_pref 0. vcodec != 'none' \u2192 else: acodec != 'none' \u2192 no penalty. prefer_free_formats \u2192 params={} \u2192 .get \u2192 None \u2192 falsy \u2192 ORDER=['webm','flv','mp4'] \u2192 ext_preference=index('mp4')=2. audio_ext_preference=0.\n\nhigh key: (0, -1, -1, 4000, -1, -1, 1080, -1, 0, 2, -1, 0, -1, -1, -1, 'http-mp4_1080')\nplain key: (0, -1, -1, -1, -1, -1, -1, -1, 0, 2, -1, 0, -1, -1, -1, 'http-mp4_other')\n\u2192 plain < high \u2192 sorted: [plain, high] \u2192 formats[-1] = high = 'http-mp4_1080' \u2713.\n\nAlso note the tbr-merge loop: `'tbr' not in f and f.get('abr') is not None and f.get('vbr') is not None` \u2014 our formats: high HAS tbr; plain has neither abr nor vbr \u2192 skip \u2713.\n\nTest 3 formats (I provide protocol/ext):\n- hls-720: ext 'mp4' provided \u2192 workaround skips. preference 0. protocol 'm3u8' \u2192 proto_pref -0