load api/other. requested = [(PAGE_URL, VIDEO_ID), ('https://video.udn.com/api/1080', VIDEO_ID), ('https://video.udn.com/api/other', VIDEO_ID)] \u2713 deterministic (py3.7+ dict order; json.loads preserves).\n\nurljoin('https://video.udn.com/embed/news/300040', '/api/1080') = 'https://video.udn.com/api/1080' \u2713 (leading slash \u2192 root).\n\nTest 3: requested = [(PAGE_URL, VIDEO_ID), ('https://video.udn.com/api/hls', VIDEO_ID), ('https://video.udn.com/api/hds', VIDEO_ID)] \u2713.\n\nNow \u2014 the m3u8/f4m mock assertions:\n- m3u8 called once with ('https://cdn.example.com/master.m3u8', VIDEO_ID) and kwargs {'ext': 'mp4', 'm3u8_id': 'hls'} \u2713 (call site: `self._extract_m3u8_formats(video_url, video_id, ext='mp4', m3u8_id='hls')`).\n- f4m called once with ('https://cdn.example.com/manifest.f4m', VIDEO_ID), kwargs {'f4m_id': 'hds'} \u2713.\n\ndetermine_ext checks:\n- 'https://cdn.example.com/master.m3u8' \u2192 'm3u8' \u2713\n- 'https://cdn.example.com/manifest.f4m' \u2192 'f4m' \u2713\n- 'https://cdn.example.com/video_1080p_4000.mp4' \u2192 'mp4' \u2713\n- 'https://cdn.example.com/video.mp4' \u2192 'mp4' \u2713\n\ndetermine_ext classic: splits url, strips query, lowercases ext... 'master.m3u8' \u2192 'm3u8' \u2713.\n\nNow the regex `_(?P<height>\\d+)p_(?P<tbr>\\d+)\\.mp4` on 'https://cdn.example.com/video_1080p_4000.mp4' \u2192 matches '_1080p_4000.mp4' \u2192 height='1080', tbr='4000' \u2192 int_or_none \u2192 1080, 4000 \u2713. On 'https://cdn.example.com/video.mp4' \u2192 no match \u2192 mobj None \u2192 no height/tbr \u2713.\n\nEverything checks out. Now the remaining get_info batch to confirm: _PROTOCOL_RELATIVE_VALID_URL, _match_id, set_downloader, determine_protocol, _html_search_regex. Let me fire those.\n\nThen write the final test.\n\nOne more thing \u2014 test for the `if not api_url: continue` branch: covered by 'mp4_broken': '' in test 2 \u2713. And I assert len(formats)==2 proving the skip.\n\nAlso \u2014 should I add a test where options parse