name, group, fatal=fatal, flags=flags)\n    ...\n```\n\nPure. But let me verify quickly \u2014 add to batch: `InfoExtractor._html_search_regex` and `InfoExtractor._search_regex`. Hmm, _search_regex might call `self._downloader` on failure... only on failure paths; our patterns match. I'll check _html_search_regex anyway to be thorough. Actually, let me check `_match_id`, `set_downloader`, `determine_protocol`, `UDNEmbedIE._PROTOCOL_RELATIVE_VALID_URL`, `InfoExtractor._html_search_regex`. 5 calls.\n\nAlso \u2014 one more: `InfoExtractor._download_webpage` \u2014 in this version, is its signature `(self, url_or_request, video_id, note=..., ...)`? The call site: `self._download_webpage(url, video_id)` and `self._download_webpage(urljoin(url, api_url), video_id, note='retrieve url for %s video' % video_type)`. My stub: `def fake(url_or_request, video_id, *args, **kwargs)` \u2014 compatible regardless. Skip.\n\nLet me also think again about `js_to_json` on my TEST 2 options string:\n\n`{'video': {'mp4_1080': '/api/1080', 'mp4_broken': '', 'mp4_other': '/api/other'}, 'title': 'Test Title', 'poster': 'https://example.com/poster.jpg'}`\n\nTrace js_to_json regex `(?sx)` over it:\n- At `{` \u2014 no match (alternatives need quote/comment/identifier/number/!) \u2192 advance.\n- `'video'` \u2014 single-quote alt: `'(?:[^'\\\\]*(?:\\\\\\\\|\\\\['\"nurtbfx/\\n]))*[^'\\\\]*'` \u2014 matches `'video'` \u2713 \u2192 fix_kv: starts with `'` \u2192 v[1:-1]='video', inner re.sub on escapes \u2014 none \u2192 return `'\"video\"'` \u2713.\n- `:` \u2014 no match.\n- ` ` \u2014 no.\n- `{` \u2014 no.\n- `'mp4_1080'` \u2192 `'\"mp4_1080\"'` \u2713\n- `:` , ` ` \u2014 no.\n- `'/api/1080'` \u2192 `'\"/api/1080\"'` \u2713 \u2014 wait, the single-quote regex: `'(?:[^'\\\\]*(?:\\\\\\\\|\\\\['\"nurtbfx/\\n]))*[^'\\\\]*'` \u2014 content `/api/1080` has no quotes/backslashes \u2713.\n- `,` \u2014 trailing-comma alt: `,(?={skip}[\\]}])` \u2014 after `,` comes ` 'mp4_broken'` \u2014 `{skip}` = `\\s*(?