ter regex: `poster\\s*:\\s*'(.+?)'\\s*,` \u2014 `poster: 'https://example.com/fallback.jpg',` \u2713 \u2192 URL.\n\n\u2713 All good. Note: `_html_search_regex` for video urls operates on trans_options_str \u2014 the regex needs `\"video\"` DOUBLE-quoted in trans \u2014 \u2713 since js_to_json quoted... wait, `\"video\"` was ALREADY double-quoted in my options_str. Even better \u2014 no reliance on key-quoting for the video dict. But title/poster keys DID rely on js_to_json quoting? No \u2014 the title/poster regexes run on options_str (ORIGINAL), where they're unquoted `title:` \u2014 the regex `title\\s*:\\s*'` doesn't care about quotes on the key \u2713. And the video regex runs on trans_options_str where `\"video\"` is double-quoted (originally so) \u2713. Robust.\n\nHmm \u2014 one more check on the video regex against trans_options_str: `({.+?})\\s*,` \u2014 non-greedy `.+?` with `(?sx)` flags? `_html_search_regex` compiles with flags=0 (unless passed). `.` won't match `\\n` \u2014 my page is single-line inside the script \u2713. But wait \u2014 the FULL page HTML: `<html><script>var options = {...};</script></html>` \u2014 the regex `\"video\"\\s*:\\s*({.+?})\\s*,` is applied to trans_options_str (just the options substring), not the whole page \u2713.\n\nAnd the options regex `var\\s+options\\s*=\\s*([^;]+);` applied to the PAGE \u2014 `[^;]+` \u2014 my options contain no `;` \u2713. But CAREFUL: `</script></html>` after the `;` \u2014 irrelevant, match ends at first `;` \u2713.\n\nNow \u2014 `_search_regex`/`_html_search_regex` \u2014 need to confirm no downloader dependency on SUCCESS path. Classic impl returns group. I'll verify with get_info to be safe.\n\nNow the remaining verification batch:\n- `UDNEmbedIE._PROTOCOL_RELATIVE_VALID_URL`\n- `InfoExtractor._match_id`\n- `InfoExtractor.set_downloader`\n- `determine_protocol`\n- `InfoExtractor._html_search_regex`\n\nLet me also grab `InfoExtractor._download_webpage` just to be 100% sure about arg names (not n