`f.get('height') is None` in the key...\n\nOh wait! Maybe the sort is `formats.sort(key=_formats_key)` where the key is such that LOWER = WORSE... and unknown height: `f.get('height') is None` \u2192 True... \n\nHmm hold on. Let me look at actual youtube-dl source from memory of the repo (common.py, circa 2023):\n\n```python\n    def _sort_formats(self, formats):\n        if not formats:\n            raise ExtractorError('No video formats found!')\n\n        def _formats_key(f):\n            # TODO remove the following workaround\n            from ..utils import determine_ext\n            if f.get('ext') in (None, 'unknown_ext'):\n                f['ext'] = determine_ext(f['url'])\n\n            # TODO move all sanitization to _sort_formats\n            protocol = f.get('protocol')\n            if protocol is None:\n                protocol = determine_protocol(f)\n            f['protocol'] = protocol\n\n            preference = f.get('preference')\n            if preference is None:\n                preference = 0\n            if self._downloader.params.get('prefer_free_formats'):\n                ORDER = [preference, f.get('height') is None, f.get('height'), f.get('tbr') is None, f.get('tbr'), f.get('vcodec') == 'none', f.get('acodec') == 'none', f.get('abr') is None, f.get('abr'), f.get('ext') in ('f4f', 'f4m'), f.get('filesize') is None, f.get('filesize')]\n            else:\n                ORDER = [preference, f.get('vcodec') == 'none', f.get('height') is None, f.get('height'), f.get('tbr') is None, f.get('tbr'), f.get('acodec') == 'none', f.get('abr') is None, f.get('abr'), f.get('ext') in ('f4f', 'f4m'), f.get('filesize') is None, f.get('filesize')]\n            return tuple(ORDER)\n\n        formats.sort(key=_formats_key)\n```\n\nHmm, I keep producing the same. But wait \u2014 this can't be right because it would make unknown-height formats best. Unless... hmm, actually maybe it IS right in a weird way: no wait.\n\nHmm, let me think about actual youtube-dl 