ol = determine_protocol(f)\n            f['protocol'] = protocol\n\n            preference = f.get('preference')\n            if preference is None:\n                preference = 0\n            if self._downloader.params.get('prefer_free_formats'):\n                ORDER = [preference, f.get('height') is None, f.get('height'), f.get('tbr') is None, f.get('tbr'), f.get('vcodec') == 'none', f.get('acodec') == 'none', f.get('abr') is None, f.get('abr'), f.get('ext') in ('f4f', 'f4m'), f.get('filesize') is None, f.get('filesize')]\n            else:\n                ORDER = [preference, f.get('vcodec') == 'none', f.get('height') is None, f.get('height'), f.get('tbr') is None, f.get('tbr'), f.get('acodec') == 'none', f.get('abr') is None, f.get('abr'), f.get('ext') in ('f4f', 'f4m'), f.get('filesize') is None, f.get('filesize')]\n            return tuple(ORDER)\n\n        formats.sort(key=_formats_key)\n```\n\nUgh, I'm going in circles. The key insight I might be missing: maybe it's `f.get('height') is not None`? Or maybe the tuple is negated? Let me just check with the tool. If get_info returns the source, great.\n\nHmm, wait, actually \u2014 I now genuinely recall that in youtube-dl there was a change: https://github.com/ytdl-org/youtube-dl/commit/... The `_sort_formats` key uses `f.get('height') is None` \u2014 hmm...\n\nOK here's another angle: think about how youtube-dl picks the default format. In `process_video_result`:\n\n```python\n        if download:\n            ...\n        req_format = self._default_format_spec(info_dict, download=download)\n        ...\n        formats_to_download = list(format_selector({'formats': formats}))\n```\n\nAnd `_build_format_selector`:\n\n```python\n    def _build_format_selector(self, format_spec):\n        def syntax_error(note, start):\n        ...\n        PICKFIRST = ...\n        ...\n        if format_spec in ('best', 'best/bv*+ba/b'):\n            ...\n```\n\nHmm, in youtube-dl:\n\n```python\n        def _parse_format_sel