me, group, fatal=fatal, flags=flags)\n    ...\n```\n\nPure. But let me verify quickly \u2014 add to batch: `InfoExtractor._html_search_regex` and `InfoExtractor._search_regex`. Hmm, _search_regex might call `self._downloader` on failure... only on failure paths; our patterns match. I'll check _html_search_regex anyway to be thorough. Actually, let me check `_match_id`, `set_downloader`, `determine_protocol`, `UDNEmbedIE._PROTOCOL_RELATIVE_VALID_URL`, `InfoExtractor._html_search_regex`. 5 calls.\n\nAlso \u2014 one more: `InfoExtractor._download_webpage` \u2014 in this version, is its signature `(self, url_or_request, video_id, note=..., ...)`? The call site: `self._download_webpage(url, video_id)` and `self._download_webpage(urljoin(url, api_url), video_id, note='retrieve url for %s video' % video_type)`. My stub: `def fake(url_or_request, video_id, *args, **kwargs)` \u2014 compatible regardless. Skip.\n\nLet me also think again about `js_to_json` on my TEST 2 options string:\n\n`{'video': {'mp4_1080': '/api/1080', 'mp4_broken': '', 'mp4_other': '/api/other'}, 'title': 'Test Title', 'poster': 'https://example.com/poster.jpg'}`\n\nTrace js_to_json regex `(?sx)` over it:\n- At `{` \u2014 no match (alternatives need quote/comment/identifier/number/!) \u2192 advance.\n- `'video'` \u2014 single-quote alt: `'(?:[^'\\\\]*(?:\\\\\\\\|\\\\['\"nurtbfx/\\n]))*[^'\\\\]*'` \u2014 matches `'video'` \u2713 \u2192 fix_kv: starts with `'` \u2192 v[1:-1]='video', inner re.sub on escapes \u2014 none \u2192 return `'\"video\"'` \u2713.\n- `:` \u2014 no match.\n- ` ` \u2014 no.\n- `{` \u2014 no.\n- `'mp4_1080'` \u2192 `'\"mp4_1080\"'` \u2713\n- `:` , ` ` \u2014 no.\n- `'/api/1080'` \u2192 `'\"/api/1080\"'` \u2713 \u2014 wait, the single-quote regex: `'(?:[^'\\\\]*(?:\\\\\\\\|\\\\['\"nurtbfx/\\n]))*[^'\\\\]*'` \u2014 content `/api/1080` has no quotes/backslashes \u2713.\n- `,` \u2014 trailing-comma alt: `,(?={skip}[\\]}])` \u2014 after `,` comes ` 'mp4_broken'` \u2014 `{skip}` = `\\s*(?:comment)?\\s*` matches ` `, then needs `[\\]}]` \u2014 `'` no \u2192 alt fails. Other alts at `,`? No. \u2192 `,` stays \u2713.\n- `'mp4_broken'` \u2192 quoted \u2713. `''` \u2192 `'\"\"'`... wait `''` \u2014 single-quote alt matches `''` (empty content) \u2192 fix_kv \u2192 `'\"\"'` \u2192 `\"\"` \u2713 valid empty string.\n- `'/api/other'` \u2192 \u2713\n- `}` `,` \u2014 after `,` comes ` 'title'` \u2014 not `]`/`}` \u2192 stays \u2713\n- `'title'` \u2192 \u2713, `'Test Title'` \u2192 `\"Test Title\"` \u2713\n- `,` `'poster'` \u2192 \u2713, `'https://example.com/poster.jpg'` \u2192 `\"https://example.com/poster.jpg\"` \u2713\n- `}` \u2014 no match.\n\nResult: `{\"video\": {\"mp4_1080\": \"/api/1080\", \"mp4_broken\": \"\", \"mp4_other\": \"/api/other\"}, \"title\": \"Test Title\", \"poster\": \"https://example.com/poster.jpg\"}` \u2192 valid JSON \u2713\u2713.\n\nWait \u2014 one catch: the identifier alternative `(?:(?<![0-9])[eE]|[a-df-zA-DF-Z_])[.a-zA-Z_0-9]*` \u2014 could it match parts INSIDE already-handled strings? No \u2014 re.sub consumes matches left-to-right; quoted strings are consumed wholly by the string alternatives when the scan reaches their opening quote. But what about text BETWEEN matches \u2014 e.g., inside `'https://example.com/poster.jpg'`, the scan hits `'` first and the single-quote alternative matches the WHOLE string \u2713. Good.\n\nHmm, but WAIT \u2014 one more subtle thing in fix_kv for single-quoted strings:\n\n```python\nif v[0] in (\"'\", '\"'):\n    v = re.sub('(?s)\\\\\\\\.|\"', lambda m: {...}.get(m.group(0), m.group(0)), v[1:-1])\nreturn '\"%s\"' % v\n```\n\nFor v = `'https://example.com/poster.jpg'`: v[1:-1] = `https://example.com/poster.jpg`; inner re.sub looks for `\\\\.` or `\"` \u2014 none \u2192 unchanged \u2192 `'\"https://example.com/poster.jpg\"'` \u2713.\n\nFor test 1 (youtube): `{'video': {'youtube': 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BaW_jenozKc'}, 'title': 'YT Title', 'poster': 'https://example.com/poster.jpg'}` \u2192